+## Opt-in account routing diagnostics
+
+A newly created sandbox can use `--log-level off,openshell.routing_http=debug`
+to enable a dedicated supervisor console diagnostic. The default is unchanged.
+Only the exact GET account-check endpoint at `chatgpt.com:443` is recognized;
+queries and absolute request targets are excluded. Each recognized request emits
+at most one terminal event with a bounded ordinal, fixed kind/method/outcome,
+and an optional final HTTP status. Headers, bodies, addresses, paths, credential
+values, and formatted errors are never included in this event.
+
+These DEBUG events may be absent from the gateway's INFO push stream. Observe
+the exact owned supervisor console before deleting its sandbox. A missing event
+is inconclusive. HTTP 200 does not prove valid account JSON or account routing;
+multiple events must retain their distinct ordinals. This diagnostic does not
+issue requests, refresh credentials, test inference, or establish model availability.
+
 ## TUI
 
